			<div class="content" id="post-content-758730">
									

<p>Okay, that big question? That's beyond the purview of the article to answer, since this is an article about the containment procedures. But let's use a hypothetical situation.</p>
<p>Let's say that in 1999, a letter was received with the appropriate code-phrase and markings from 14 September, 2001. In it, there is information about 9/11, with the edict that all information the Foundation has stored in the World Trade Center is to be backed up and taken to Site 17 at the end of business, 10 September, 2001. Nothing about saving personnel, mind you, just the information.</p>
<p>Imagine the havoc that could be caused by the Foundation knowing about the events two years beforehand. That's why it's Overseers only, to minimize temporal disruption.</p>
<p>Occasionally, orders like that will be given and directed as stated. However, the Foundation is a profoundly paranoid organization, and as such has a variety of safeguards in place to minimize such shenanigans. Again, that's beyond the article's purview, but I should at least be hinting at that sort of thinking and double-thinking here, no?</p>

							</div>

								
					
